# Test: RFC 4271 Section 6.2 -- an OPEN whose AS is not the configured remote AS
# is refused with OPEN Message Error (2) / Bad Peer AS (2).
# VALIDATES: ze compares the AS a peer opens with against `session asn remote`
#            (validateOpenPeerAS, internal/component/bgp/reactor/session_open_as.go)
#            and answers a mismatch with NOTIFICATION 2/2, with no Data field,
#            before the session establishes.
# PREVENTS: the tolerance ze had before RFC 7705 Section 4.2 work landed, when any
#           AS was accepted because nothing compared it. A peer configured for
#           65001 that opens with 65099 is a misconfiguration the operator must be
#           told about, not a session.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: with the comparison removed, ze accepts 65099, answers with a
# KEEPALIVE, and the NOTIFICATION below never arrives.
#
# The dynamic-peer exemption (AC-3 of spec-bgp-as-migration) needs no file of its
# own: every dynamic-group .ci (dynamic-group-static-peer-wins.ci among them)
# establishes a session whose remote AS is unknown until OPEN, which a check
# without the exemption would refuse.

# ze-peer expectations
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=10s
# Open with 65099, an AS ze is not configured for.
option=asn:value=65099
# Expect NOTIFICATION: OPEN Message Error (code 2), Bad Peer AS (subcode 2)
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0015030202
EOF_PEER

# ze bgp configuration -- an ordinary eBGP peer with no migration AS
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=10s
